{"title":"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Factors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Factors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Decimals)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Decimals)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Really_thorough)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Really thorough)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Intuition_for_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Intuition for Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> denote the value of the infinite sum \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/3165cd4665a68f08a66005bca86a0224dd53b6f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{99}+\\frac{1}{999}+\\frac{1}{9999}+\\dots.\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"37\" />\nFind the remainder when the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/1209e768d4258beb06712e870f8a5ab3e2f10fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{100}S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Expressing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> algebraically, we can write\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd6bf51aba2ab9a310844e0bf41cd41bd5d2793.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=\\sum_{a\\ge1}\\frac{1}{10^a-1}=\\sum_{a\\ge1}\\sum_{b\\ge1}10^{-ab}.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"47\" />\nThe term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e2cf91f2c46fb67da50f124b4127cd36b736b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> will appear exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456f051f0d6a8b0f2745b1cd63a4b26003858880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> times in the above sum: this is because the divisor function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456f051f0d6a8b0f2745b1cd63a4b26003858880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> counts the number of ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f0e9b41743e7fa2d4493b18643ef67485929c07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb7ab26c7b508eb4b5143358872597c1441fa3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />. So we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4375b519f7c9c17c761c232ca44653c7d82a1b55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=\\sum_{n\\ge 1}\\tau(n)10^{-n},\\quad10^{100}S = \\sum_{n\\ge 1}\\tau(n)10^{100-n}.\\]\" width=\"362\" height=\"40\" />\nThe sum of all terms with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/749d949bbc25017ebc3df68b3862430e44b1af16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so it is negligible. Hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd92fc47c9fa0358575b48385a272950dd4cf416.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor 10^{100}S\\rfloor \\equiv \\sum_{n=1}^{100}\\tau(n)10^{100-n}\\equiv\\tau(98)\\cdot 100+\\tau(99)\\cdot 10+\\tau(100)\\equiv \\boxed{669} \\pmod{1000}.\\]\" width=\"629\" height=\"50\" />\n~TThB0501\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Factors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Factors)\">Solution 2 (Factors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Factors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After a bit of thinking, you'll realize that for each digit after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a244e37e0be72b5bbb630061463daa61144b76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> is the number of factors of that digit.\n</p><p>So we're basically looking for the number of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60be3b3c9ba5689293a9710eb155b77751d3f6d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98,99,100 ($\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> to check for carried ones<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d62387987dc59220a2f25413fb9133a14dc32737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1dadfe7423df0427cf54d29f2559b025f1fba13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98 = 2\\cdot7^2, 99 = 11\\cdot3^2, 100 = 2^2\\cdot5^2, 101 = 101, 98 \\to{2\\cdot3=6}, 99 \\to{2\\cdot3=6}, 100 \\to{3\\cdot3=9}, 101 \\to{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"818\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>So, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/e/8ce1e528512ad0d978a5c919dfab8363d28c58c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$669$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The two doesn't carry a one, therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/391f46cb60e45e54965ddb15caeb1c17b18d9e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{669}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"45\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~ BenjaminDong01\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Decimals.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Decimals)\">Solution 3 (Decimals)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Decimals)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can represent each of the terms as a recurring decimal. \n</p><p>For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd17652a2c83a885545739261548569710aa7ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{9} = 0.\\overline{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/789cd4a49734099afffe8024246cdc07ee594b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{99} = 0.\\overline{01}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />. Given this it is trivial to see that the only terms that will contribute to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45b677aee4bcc6ec8da6be5021e8b3abe9635b0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$nth$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> decimal place will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822482b16a7aa9444e91b3928b31deef99827268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10^a - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"63\" height=\"40\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>Now consider multiplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b41aee75eee4f322b88a22ab66cf7565f94e27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> and taking it modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. This would leave the digits in the 98th, 99th, and 100th places. \n</p><p>So, we find that 98 has 6 factors, 99 has 6 factors, and 100 has 9 factors. 101 is prime, so we don't need to worry about any carrying affecting the 100th decimal place. \n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076e47ede663bd3747827b89445c0cf2a40643ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{669}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~mathmaniak\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Really_thorough.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Really_thorough)\">Solution 4 (Really thorough)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Really thorough)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is very well known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74c46ec255acbe75dc761b9b9c3c1a81d8fa3a69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{10^n-1}=0.\\overline{\\underbrace{00...00}_{\\text{ n-1 zeros}}a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"172\" height=\"46\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/9656ef8ab5d863dbc427285702455d17483301d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[T_n=\\frac{1}{10^n-1}=0.\\overline{\\underbrace{00...00}_{\\text{ n-1 zeros}}1}\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4f0aad03683fbcd9ece700707f768eeac33c9e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k=\\sum_{n=0}^k(T_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"105\" height=\"56\" />, \n</p><p>The problem asks us for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e064b31bb86f2a4bd8b87f960944ec031ba2107.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor10^{100}S_\\infty\\rfloor\\pmod{1000}\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2eacbcb991af87d495f8689ac0e952b51317dbaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1af718e06e4790f48530b482fb93943abd01373d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-th$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> place value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fca2a200c46295df67c289636646e9bda4ef1edd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />, before converting. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e2f964c583e39c78bdb2a50d09a317521d48cca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{48}=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />.\nObserve that each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f4341a1efbe1a890de160de023b4e4b84ef444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is periodic with period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Then, it sbould be obvious that each value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f9623f3f5745c7a7eed3bcfa81adcc294f7524d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{kn}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f2156b0a731a63b7df0ddbe84b3dbb0c7418cd36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in\\mathbb{Z^+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />) has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> contributed from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f4341a1efbe1a890de160de023b4e4b84ef444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f4341a1efbe1a890de160de023b4e4b84ef444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> \"deposits\" as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> digits.  \n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>We can therefore say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30a4c3918ef76dffd4a54339ddfafdbe97d5916c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_n=\\sigma_0(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a5070149b154210d0ebe3ef9955452553a4560d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma_0(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> is the number of divisors of n. In general, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2c405acafdc713290b5411aa22c17768cea6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma_k(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> is the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4e10b96abb203b2cbaed76cdb339fbc71d62aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-th$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> powers of the divisors n)\n</p><p>I think we can agree that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fbf9b6f14d9e415338f0478032ad35db3f9629a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_\\infty=\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty(\\frac{D^n}{10^n})=\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty(\\frac{\\sigma_0(n)}{10^n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"233\" height=\"53\" /> from the definition of place values.\n</p><p>We can also argue that the terms after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/f/37fb444c8a7d6e4636e2592d29717e4419d8743f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> are inconsequential. This is basically because it is easy enough to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a5070149b154210d0ebe3ef9955452553a4560d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma_0(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> is much less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8793942960a87f6920c08986ef92cde0f52a3f45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{n-100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/749d949bbc25017ebc3df68b3862430e44b1af16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, and summing all of those values is logically not going to be over 1. IE, those terms will never \"escape the decimal place\". Then, the floor part will just remove that.\n</p><p>So we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/898ca656e5760846a41edc3253756777bb501bb8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor10^{100}S_\\infty\\rfloor=10^{100}S_{100}=10^{100}\\sum_{n=0}^{100}(\\frac{\\sigma_0(n)}{10^n})\\]\" width=\"323\" height=\"50\" />\nWe want: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239bd47f9115e7464b2d08201b2c3aa2a84bf193.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10^{100}\\sum_{n=0}^{100}(\\frac{\\sigma_0(n)}{10^n})\\pmod{1000}\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Since we are working mod 1000, all of the terms with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/1736f2c85c38f3d9032560c0161389ba1f19bd90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\leq97$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> will end up as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43fa626885ed755cb01ba0cc8e1caa719e87b8cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma_0(n)*10^{(r\\geq3)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"23\" />. So, all of the terms just disappear before n=98. We are then left with: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da141d143a84b4b1b41f892143e635bc2edfd43.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{\\sigma_0(98)}*{10^{(100-98)}}+{\\sigma_0(99)}*{10^{(100-99)}}+{\\sigma_0(100)}*{10^{(100-100)}}=6*100+6*10+9=\\boxed{669}\\]\" width=\"646\" height=\"23\" /> Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6ddfa520874aee8b77682c3326e038c055f006ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98=2*49=2^1*7^2\\therefore\\sigma_0(98)=2*3=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"328\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a697f7c713b60d51e7bb9a4cb5dd7c2a80452845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99=9*11=3^2*11^2\\therefore\\sigma_0(99)=2*3=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"337\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5617eccb11a3ef286c7c5ff14123b09ebddf3166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100=4*25=2^2*5^2\\therefore\\sigma_0(100)=3*3=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"346\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>~Stereotypicalmathnerd\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Intuition_for_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Intuition_for_Solution_1)\">Solution 5 (Intuition for Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Intuition for Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we see that we just have the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/352827f81e99bc1361f76ce6e8b1a741e629d2a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{10^k - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"92\" height=\"53\" />. We factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfdcd69788aebdb2c3ccbdeee64480267b6fd927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> at the bottom to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/2/e822cca159b9de13f7d960c1ea65dbd06b1e8025.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{10^k(1 - 10^{-k})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"143\" height=\"53\" />. We replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/609c5ab71678b57fc21bab3d7a3bc354244cd69f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10^k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"32\" height=\"38\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00ee7eceb4f1d85619fab0ed34e150838ac03a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{-k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> and the result is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1c65aafc2f85a7d408fd31c5a358960c52cbb70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{10^{-k}}{1 - 10^{-k}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"103\" height=\"53\" />. However, that result is just an infinite geometric series! We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a20d488012479935a87014e68893cb6760d1fc8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 10^{-k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d38fde9a9989c0afaad8563259563d3af59909c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; |r| &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />. The first term of this series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> itself. Thus, the series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/a/21a33d1dbb2de9db151f8fa3b2c6374637991239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> for some values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, and we can conclude the sum as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e062d8fee923698e091bcbb30361bdfc0548c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{l=1}^{\\infty} (10^{-k})^l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"83\" height=\"53\" />. We determine the value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> using an exterior nested sum to obtain the double sum found in solution 1. Continue as followed.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MadMath\">Video Solution by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wurQ53M3f6M\">https://youtu.be/wurQ53M3f6M</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II\" title=\"2026 AIME II\">2026 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2026 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017042550\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 489/1000000\nPost‐expand include s